Mandol Multimodal is derived from Mandol, the open-source agent memory system
maintained by the Mandol Team (https://github.com/AgentCombo/Mandol).
The upstream project is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0;
see LICENSE for the license text.

Original technical report:
Yuhan Zhang, Zhiyuan Guo, Ziheng Zeng, Wei Wang, Wentao Wu, and Lijie Xu.
"Mandol: An Agglomerative Agent Memory System for Long-Term Conversations."
arXiv:2606.29778 (2026), https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.29778.

Multimodal-track modifications in this repository add an AML Add/Search/Health
adapter, strict image ingestion, per-user original-image storage, a replaceable
visual extraction interface, deterministic text rendering into L0 MemoryUnits,
SQLite-backed idempotent writes and graph recovery, and ranked multimodal
evidence reconstruction. The upstream Mandol retrieval implementation remains
unchanged. The mock extractor and local tests are not an official AML result.
